[gd_scene load_steps=14 format=3]

; THE OPEN LAGOON (REQ-009) — the hub, as a scene, and the game's main scene.
;
; Deliberately empty of portals: every pedestal is BUILT at runtime by
; open_lagoon.gd from what the registry discovers under worlds/. A portal
; authored into this file would be a hardcoded world list in disguise, which
; is exactly what AC-1 forbids.
;
; STRUCTURE. The player and camera are SIBLINGS of the OpenLagoon node, not
; children: the hub disables its own subtree while a world is active (hiding
; is not enough — an invisible floor still collides), and a player parented
; under it would freeze mid-world. Whatever survives a world transition lives
; beside the hub, never inside it. The LIGHTING RIG is the third such sibling:
; the shared environment and sun (core/rendering/world_lighting.tscn) light the
; hub AND every world entered from it, which only works because they are not
; under the subtree the hub switches off.

